📄 Document Processing Module

📌 Overview

The Document Processing Module is responsible for receiving, validating, extracting, cleaning, and preparing information from documents for further processing in the project.

It acts as an initial stage of the system by converting uploaded documents into structured and usable text/data.

🎯 Objectives

- 📤 Accept uploaded documents
- ✅ Validate document type and format
- 📖 Extract text from documents
- 🧹 Clean and preprocess extracted text
- 🔍 Identify useful information from documents
- 📊 Convert unstructured document content into structured data
- 🔗 Provide processed data to the next module

🔄 Document Processing Workflow

Document Upload
       ↓
File Validation
       ↓
Document Reading
       ↓
Text Extraction
       ↓
Text Cleaning
       ↓
Data Preprocessing
       ↓
Structured Output
       ↓
Further Processing

🛠️ Technologies Used

- Python
- FastAPI – API development
- PyPDF2 / pypdf – PDF text extraction
- python-docx – Word document processing
- Pandas – Data processing
- Regular Expressions (Regex) – Text cleaning and pattern extraction

📂 Module Responsibilities

1. File Upload

The module accepts documents uploaded by the user through the application/API.

Supported formats can include:

- PDF
- DOCX
- TXT

2. File Validation

The uploaded file is checked for:

- Valid file format
- File extension
- File size
- Empty or corrupted files

3. Text Extraction

Text is extracted from the uploaded document depending on its format.

For example:

PDF → Extract text from PDF pages
DOCX → Extract paragraphs from Word document
TXT → Read text directly

4. Text Cleaning

The extracted text is cleaned to remove unnecessary content such as:

- Extra spaces
- Unwanted special characters
- Empty lines
- Duplicate spaces
- Formatting inconsistencies

5. Data Preprocessing

The cleaned document content is prepared for further processing.

Example:

Raw Document
     ↓
Extracted Text
     ↓
Cleaned Text
     ↓
Processed Data

